0001   0000             ; Emission past the top of the image.
0002   0000             ;
0003   0000             ; The counter is not clamped: .ORG and the counter hold any value. A byte whose
0004   0000             ; address exceeds $FFFF is wrapped to 16 bits and still emitted, so the run
0005   0000             ; stays one object record rather than splitting -- five bytes from $FFFC is a
0006   0000             ; five-byte record at FFFC. The listing shows the counter unmasked, five digits,
0007   0000             ; which pushes the source column right by one.
0008   0000             ;
0009   0000             ; By default the first out-of-range address is diagnosed, once per run.
0010   0000             ; --bug-compatibility restores the original's silence. Assembled both ways.
0011   FFFC                     .org  $FFFC
0012   FFFC 01 00 02 00         .dw   1,2
